    "reading_doc61_SS9_2": "the per-WIRE trace is read against doc 61 SS9.2's PRE-COMPUTED INVENTORY as its baseline, NOT against 1: a generic unit vector in R^{2^q} is not a product of q single-qubit states, so the intro per-wire purity is below 1 BY CONSTRUCTION and is a DATA-DETERMINED CONSTANT OF THE ENCODING, not a circuit effect. A3 min/median/max 0.5036/0.6660/0.9693; A4 0.5046/0.5299/0.7924; NO NOUN IS WITHIN 0.05 OF A PRODUCT STATE at either rung. Here the mechanism is MAXIMAL AND UNAVOIDABLE, and it is the ENCODING, not a gate.",
    "registered_question_doc61_SS9_4": "does the readout restore the per-REGISTER purity to its INTRO value (1.0, by construction) on correct q = 2 items and fail to on q = 1 items -- the q-asymmetry undo signature (doc 55 SS20.5) transposed from wires to registers? DESCRIPTIVE, NO BOOLEAN, NO CRITERION. The healthy committed profile is the wire-level one (R2-A: 0.8755 vs 0.8751 on correct q = 2; 0.8017 vs 0.8953 on q = 1).",
